      "writtenOn": "2020-01-23T15:34:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think that sdkCore is a separate kind. I think it is orthogonal to that. Core is essentially just a partition of the public API space that relates to the core libraries, i.e. art, i18n and conscrypt.\n\nSimilarly, core_platform is a partition of the \"platform\" kind. Where \"platform\" is more akin to \"private\" than any of the others.\n\nI think core would be better represented by adding another field to sdkSpec, say partition, so core_current would be \"public\", \"core\", \"current\", core_platform would be \"private\", \"core\", \"current\" and system_current would be \"system\", \"\u003csomething, maybe base or an empty string\u003e\", \"current\".",
      "revId": "698d6c7e9b4d435f21000b37fa5a998b2a6a83ce",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
